// RUN CANARY (exit 11). BUILD-PRODUCT-REFERENCES customer: the package
// carries two modules whose product declarations share the boundary-trait
// leaf spelling (`left::Reader`/`right::Reader`) and a distractor
// runner/provider pair under `right` (`RightRunner`, `RightProvider`
// computing 37). The build describes `left::Runner::run` through
// `builder.product.entry`, a build helper returns the `ProductEntryRef`, and
// `builder.roots.bind` consumes the delegated description -- never a
// re-looked-up name. The selected identity must be the left module's exact
// machine: `run` observes its provider's computed result through the
// ordinary `main.reader.read()` call and the state branch, then exits with
// it, so a swapped or leaf-only selection would exit 37 or 65 instead of 11.
// The sibling's attached data carry tagged leaves on purpose: same-leaf
// `Runner`/`Provider` declarations still trip leaf-keyed attachment lookups
// in terminal_unit admission and composed-unit lowering, which is tracked
// under the state-local value frontier, not this item.
use left;
use right;
